* APPENDIX F CHECKING TEMPLATE - BEM INPUT DAT FILE
* Numbered notes are comments. Keep the asterisk in column 1.
* All lengths use the selected DAT unit; stresses are MPa in SI units.
TITLE
* [01] TITLE: up to 80 characters; must be the first module.
APPENDIX F CHECK - RECTANGULAR CAVITY, PLANE P WAVE

TYPE.PROBLEM
DOMAIN ANALYSIS UNITS
* [02] DOMAIN ANALYSIS UNITS: 1=Laplace transient, 2=direct time domain (original TD kernels), 3=elastostatic, 4=steady-state Laplace, 5=BDF2 convolution-quadrature time domain (ZONES required).
* [03] ANALYSIS: 1=plane strain, 2=plane stress. UNITS: 1=SI, 2=imperial, 3=user combination.
  1  1  1

SECTION.TYPE
* BOUNDARIES: number of closed/open boundaries.
BOUNDARIES
  1
SHAPE REGION ELEMENTS YELEMENTS GEOMETRY
* SHAPE: 1=ellipse/circle, 2=square, 3=rectangle, 4=straight line,
*         -n=compound boundary made from n connected segments.
* REGION: 1=cavity/external closed surface; 2=inclusion/internal closed surface;
*          3=open surface; 4=open free surface; 5/6 enclosing surfaces.
* ELEMENTS: ellipse total; square elements per side; rectangle X-side elements; line total.
* YELEMENTS: rectangle Y-side elements only.
* GEOMETRY depends on SHAPE:
*   Square (SHAPE=2): XSIDE XC YC ROT TYP DIS.
*     XSIDE=side length; XC,YC=centre; ROT=counter-clockwise rotation;
*     TYP=element grading; DIS=corner treatment (1 shared, 2 duplicated).
*   Rectangle (SHAPE=3): XSIDE YSIDE XC YC ROT TYPX TYPY DIS.
*     XSIDE/YSIDE=side lengths; XC,YC=centre; ROT=rotation;
*     TYPX/TYPY=grading on the two directions; DIS=corner treatment.
*   Circle (SHAPE=1, equal axes): ELEMENTS RADIUS XC YC ROT.
*     ROT is normally zero; the circle is centred at (XC,YC).
*   Ellipse (SHAPE=1, unequal axes): ELEMENTS XSIDE YSIDE XC YC ROT.
*     XSIDE and YSIDE are the full major/minor-axis lengths; ROT rotates
*     the ellipse counter-clockwise. (Use the geometry order required by
*     the selected PREBEM version when an ellipse is being entered.)
*   Straight open surface (SHAPE=-1): -1 REGION ELEMENTS X1 Y1 X2 Y2.
*     (X1,Y1) and (X2,Y2) are the end points; use REGION=3 or 4 for an
*     open/free surface. The element length is the total line length divided
*     by ELEMENTS.
*   Compound boundary (SHAPE=-n): -n REGION followed by n segment records.
*     Each line segment record is SHAPE=4, ELEMENTS, X1 Y1 X2 Y2; connected
*     segments must meet end-to-start. Closed compounds must return to the
*     first point; open compounds use REGION=3 or 4.
* XSIDE is the positive length of the local-x sides; YSIDE is the positive
* length of the local-y sides. XC,YC are the rectangle centre coordinates.
* ROT is the counter-clockwise angle in degrees from global +X to local +X;
* local +Y is the corresponding counter-clockwise perpendicular direction.
* The four corners are generated from local coordinates (+/-XSIDE/2,
* +/-YSIDE/2), then rotated by ROT and translated by (XC,YC).
* For a cavity (region=1), the boundary is traversed clockwise so the cavity
* remains on the enclosed side; other region/open-surface conventions follow
* the REGION code and may reverse the traversal and outward normal.
* TYP=1 uniform; p>1 grades progressively; 0<p<1 reverses the progression;
* p<-1 grades toward both corners; -1<p<0 uses the reciprocal ratio.
* TYPY=0 asks the original program to calculate the matching Y grading.
* DIS=1 shared corners; DIS=2 duplicated corners for discontinuous corner stresses.
* Example:
* SHAPE ELEMENTS YELEMENTS GEOMETRY
*   3       11       9     6.0 4.0 0.0 0.0 0.0 -2 -2  2
*     Since SHAPE=3 (Rectangle), GEOMETRY: XSIDE YSIDE XC YC ROT TYPX TYPY DIS
*   3  	  11  	   9  6.0  4.0  0.0  0.0  0.0  3.0  2.54  2

MATERIAL.PROPERTIES
